1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Fixed-price presale?
The founder picks the price.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:11,000
On the curve, the founder bids just before you.
Same budget, more tokens.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:18,000
In our auction, the bids set one price.
You both get 125,000 tokens.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Each identity bids once. Our public testnet
bidder used a stand-in Agent ID.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Our Factory created this Launcher.

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
One bidder committed 4.45 test BNB.

7
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,000
After close, anyone can settle.

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,000
That call launches through Flap if the pool
qualifies.

9
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Otherwise, bidders can claim full refunds.

10
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:50,000
I give my AI agent one BNB and two price limits.
It previews both against the local bids.

11
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:57,000
At the higher limit, my one BNB buys fifty
thousand tokens.

12
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:04,000
The agent prepares an unsigned bid.
I review it before signing.

13
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Now I lower only my limit. The clearing
price stays at 0.00002.

14
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:18,000
My bid gets zero tokens and the whole BNB
back.

15
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Back on public testnet, that single bid
funded a real launch.

16
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Settlement opened a PancakeSwap V2 pool

17
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:34,000
with half a million UNIFORM and 4.45 test
BNB.

18
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:41,000
Here is the fifth transaction. The bidder
claimed the other half million tokens.

19
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,000
We built the Launcher interface using
Flap’s template.

20
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,000
The public launch linked the Vault.

21
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:55,000
On a separate fork, trading fees reached it
and the owner withdrew them.

22
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Our code is public for both the Flap and
Developer tracks.
